  "details": "I recently started up VRC last night with the new update excited to see the hand tracking but I have to say I already hate it with a burning passion with the multiple issues/bugs I have had so far.\n\n1. Starting up VRC it forced me into hand tracking, not bad but it disabled my controllers, I could not interact with anything or open my menus which forced me to turn on hand tracking on the Vive XR Elite and figure out how to interact with the menus and figure out how to move and navigate to turn off the hand tracking.  This took 30 minutes as there was no tutorials and being hard dunked into this absolutely bricked my experience with handtracking.\n\n2. My controls need to have their bindings updated as it absolutely bricked the community XR Elite bindings I had in place. I have touch functionality on the trigger and thumbstick but it has been disabled and placed me into using Index bindings. Avatar gestures no longer properly work, I used to be able to place my pointer finger on the trigger and have the hands slightly curl, same with the thumbstick making a peace gesture no longer works. Losing half of the gesture functionality/native eye tracking in the process.\n\n3. I can no longer move my menus, forcing me to take awkward positions sometimes to access my menus. This wouldn't be so bad if the laser now is HORRIBLY not centered, often having to aim much higher than the menu to be able to click on something or interact with any world menus. Sometimes I have to give up and contort my wrists in order to get it to be accurate enough. Often times this ends up with the laser disappearing leaving me to guess wherever the heck I am clicking, often times respawning myself due to it. \n\nThis is probably a massive L on my end as I probably ain't changing certain settings but I absolutely despise this update.",
